<div class="mb-8">
  <Heading size="2xl" as="h1" class="mb-2">Image</Heading>
  <Text size="lg" tone="subdued" as="h2">
    Renders an image from the Rails asset pipeline with explicit dimensions, preventing layout
    shift while the image loads.
  </Text>
</div>

<!-- Canonical example -->
<div class="mb-8">
  <Example source={'
    <Image asset="logo.svg" width=64 height=64 alt="Orbital logo"/>
  '}/>
</div>

<!-- Usage -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Usage</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-card overflow-hidden">
    <CodeBlock code={"<Image asset=\"logo.svg\" width=64 height=64 alt=\"Orbital logo\"/>"}/>
  </div>
  <Prose class="mt-4">
    <p>
      The <code>asset</code> prop is resolved through the Rails asset pipeline, so you pass the
      logical path (e.g. <code>logo.svg</code>, <code>photos/hero.jpg</code>) rather than a full
      URL. The component generates an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> tag with the fingerprinted asset URL.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- When to Use -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">When to Use</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Use the Image component for any image served from the asset pipeline — logos, illustrations,
      avatars, and decorative graphics. The explicit <code>width</code> and <code>height</code>
      attributes reserve space in the layout before the image loads, eliminating cumulative layout
      shift (CLS).
    </p>
    <p>
      For user-uploaded content or images from external URLs, use a plain <code>&lt;img&gt;</code>
      tag instead, since those aren't served through the asset pipeline.
    </p>
    <p>
      For small symbolic graphics, prefer the <a href="/components/icon">Icon</a> component — it
      renders inline SVGs that scale with text and inherit <code>currentColor</code>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Behaviour -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Behaviour</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      The component renders a standard <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> element with
      <code>display: inline-block</code>. The <code>width</code> and <code>height</code> props
      map directly to HTML attributes, which browsers use to calculate the intrinsic aspect ratio
      before the image loads.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because the asset path is resolved at render time via <code>asset_path</code>, images benefit
      from Rails' asset fingerprinting and CDN cache headers automatically.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Examples -->
<div class="flex flex-col gap-12 mb-12">
  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Different Sizes</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>The <code>width</code> and <code>height</code> props set the rendered dimensions in pixels.
        For responsive behaviour, combine with CSS classes like <code>max-w-full</code>.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex items-end gap-6">
        <Image asset="logo.svg" width=32 height=32 alt="Small logo"/>
        <Image asset="logo.svg" width=64 height=64 alt="Medium logo"/>
        <Image asset="logo.svg" width=128 height=128 alt="Large logo"/>
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">With Styling</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Add Tailwind classes for rounded corners, borders, shadows, or other visual treatments.
        The component passes through all HTML attributes to the underlying <code>&lt;img&gt;</code>.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6">
        <Image asset="logo.svg" width=64 height=64 alt="Rounded" class="rounded-lg"/>
        <Image asset="logo.svg" width=64 height=64 alt="Circular" class="rounded-full"/>
        <Image asset="logo.svg" width=64 height=64 alt="Bordered" class="rounded-lg border-2 shadow-md"/>
      </div>
    '}/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Best Practices -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Best Practices</Heading>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-green-500/30 bg-green-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-green-600">Do</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Always provide a descriptive <code>alt</code> text for meaningful images.</li>
          <li>Set <code>width</code> and <code>height</code> to the image's actual dimensions to prevent layout shift.</li>
          <li>Use SVGs for logos and icons — they scale without loss of quality.</li>
          <li>Use <code>alt=""</code> for purely decorative images so screen readers skip them.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-red-600">Don't</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Omit the <code>alt</code> prop — an empty string is fine for decorative images, but missing alt is an accessibility violation.</li>
          <li>Use this component for external URLs — it only works with the asset pipeline.</li>
          <li>Set dimensions that distort the image's aspect ratio.</li>
          <li>Use large raster images for small display sizes — serve appropriately sized assets.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- API Reference -->
<div>
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">API Reference</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Prop</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Type</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Values</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Default</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y">
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">asset</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Asset pipeline path</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">required</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">alt</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any text</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">""</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">width</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Integer</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Pixels</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">32</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">height</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Integer</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Pixels</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">32</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
